# Test - payoffs [calc]

- dark

/*
This is an example of a "payoff diagram". The syntax is still a bit fluid, because it is quite hard to write as is.
I think it will be somewhat clear what this does if you paste it. At some point I will add extensive documentation,
but before I want to figure out what this is for. Not even I do know.
*/

Quit Quit Job

*=_Llama Open a llama farm
*=_Promo Stay, go for promotion

Quit -> *=_Llama 80% \l yes
Quit -> *=_Promo 20% \l no

*=_Llama -> *=_llama_farm_success 70% \n success
*=_Llama -> *=_llama_farm_failure 30% \n failure

*=_Promo -> *=_promo_success 50% \n success
*=_Promo -> *=_promo_failure 50% \n fail

*=_llama_farm_success -> :=_HappyLlama 500000
*=_llama_farm_failure -> :=_SadLlama -100000

*=_promo_success -> :=_HappyPromo 10000
*=_promo_failure -> :=_SadPromo 0

:=_HappyLlama -> +_LlamaPayoff
:=_SadLlama -> +_LlamaPayoff

:=_HappyPromo -> +_PromoPayoff
:=_SadPromo -> +_PromoPayoff

+_LlamaPayoff \n Potential payoff; color="sdgreen" penwidth=3
+_PromoPayoff \n Potential payoff; color="sdred" penwidth=3
